ndependent and have relatively small file size. the examples are: swf, svg, wmf, ps
\par brass_ibrahim: Vector graphics is the use of geometrical primitives such as points, lines, curves, and shapes or polygon(s), which are all based on mathematical equations, to represent images in computer graphics.
\par brass_ibrahim: The term "vector graphics" is mainly used today in the context of two-dimensional computer graphics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf11\insrsid6430109\charrsid6430109  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
